{"id": "ee847672-7a9a-42ad-9f5e-f5c83c6463d4", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "This is a SageMaker question rather than AWS DevOps Agent territory, and I don't have verify_aws_claim in my toolset, so I'll answer from what I know: yes, provisioned concurrency is designed exactly for addressing cold starts in serverless inference.

I should note it's GA since 2023, requires setting a ProvisionedConcurrency value within MaxConcurrency, and incurs billing for both the reserved capacity and actual usage -- worth flagging that I can't verify current pricing specifics. If their idle pattern is predictable, scheduling provisioned concurrency via Application Auto Scaling ahead of busy periods could be a smart alternative to running it constantly, and if traffic is actually steady, a real-time endpoint might be simpler than serverless altogether.

"}]}
